# Employee Data ETL Pipeline Using Python

A modular Python-based **ETL (Extract, Transform, Load) pipeline** that processes employee records from a CSV file, performs data cleaning and validation, detects duplicate records, and generates separate output files for valid and rejected employees.

The project includes **Python logging** to track pipeline execution, successful processing, rejected records and job-level failures.

## 1. Project Architecture

![Employee ETL Pipeline Architecture](architecture.png)

### Data Flow

```text
employees.csv
      |
      v
Extract (extract.py)
      |
      v
Transform & Validate (transform.py)
      |
      v
Duplicate Detection (main.py)
      |
      v
Load (load.py)
      |
      +----> valid_employees.csv
      |
      +----> rejected_employees.csv

main.py ---> logs/etl.log
```

The `main.py` script orchestrates the ETL workflow and manages logging.

