## 7. Logging Implementation

The pipeline uses Python's built-in `logging` module to monitor execution.

Logs are stored in:

```text
logs/etl.log
```

### Logging Features

- Pipeline start and completion messages.
- Successful employee processing.
- Warnings for invalid and duplicate records.
- Valid and rejected record counts.
- Exception details and tracebacks for unexpected pipeline failures.
- Timestamped execution history.

### Logging Configuration

```python
logging.basicConfig(
    filename=LOG_DIR / "etl.log",
    filemode="a",
    level=logging.INFO,
    format="%(asctime)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s"
)
```

### Example Logs

```text
INFO - Employee ETL pipeline started
INFO - Employee ID 101 processed successfully
INFO - Employee ID 102 processed successfully
WARNING - Employee ID 103 rejected: Invalid salary
WARNING - Employee ID 104 rejected: Salary cannot be negative
INFO - Employee ID 105 processed successfully
WARNING - Employee ID 102 rejected: Duplicate employee ID
INFO - Employee ID 106 processed successfully
INFO - Valid records: 4
INFO - Rejected records: 3
INFO - Employee ETL pipeline completed successfully
```

The actual log file also contains timestamps.

